{"name":"Guadalajara","slug":"guadalajara","region":"Latin America","lat":20.67,"lon":-103.35,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Guadalajara has warmed by about 0.15 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.3 °C in all. There is a strong, well-established El Niño effect on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run cooler, and El Niño accounts for about 15% of the year-to-year ups and downs. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 90% of a normal year-to-year swing. Without El Niño, a Dec–Feb this cool would come about once every 6 years. El Niño moves the coldest days most: this season they are expected to shift by about -0.9 °C, against -0.2 °C for the hottest days. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. Humidity shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a cooler-than-normal season is more likely than not (about 60%), about 0.3 °C below the 1991–2020 average; a wetter-than-normal season is likely (about 80% chance), and a more humid season than normal is likely (about 80% chance). This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":17.2043,"trend_per_decade":0.1725,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.2938,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.2838,"enso_p":0.0013,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.1348,"intrinsic_sd":0.674,"effect_this_season":-0.6244,"effect_ratio":0.9264,"size":"Substantial","size_typical_el_nino":"Substantial","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":6.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":-0.2685,"p_below":0.6185,"p_near":0.2019,"p_above":0.1796,"forecast_words":"More likely than not (62%): a cooler-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":-36.1966,"values":[16.776,17.713,16.351,16.774,16.432,16.211,18.174,15.847,16.206,16.173,16.111,17.29,16.407,16.011,15.77,14.934,15.641,15.903,16.814,16.017,17.138,16.984,16.912,16.885,16.05,16.208,16.341,16.375,16.892,16.102,16.384,17.438,14.758,16.527,16.442,16.649,15.946,17.578,17.858,16.44,17.156,15.443,17.127,17.844,18.508,17.453,17.204,16.005,18.022,17.169,17.783,17.6,17.276,16.011,16.9,17.802,16.397,17.636,17.602,15.719,16.855,17.577,17.786,16.74,17.236,17.177,18.002,17.151,17.342,17.605,17.851,17.922,18.049,17.583,18.639],"forecast_mean":16.9357,"forecast_sd":0.7252,"fit":{"a2027":17.5602,"b":-0.2838,"c":0.0173,"tercile_low":17.1544,"tercile_high":17.6006},"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.1632,"trend_p":0.0088,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.4211,"enso_p":0.0001,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":-0.9264,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1585,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.2894,"enso_p":0.0035,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":-0.6366,"lines_cross":false},"p95":